A||||7||88formula||Fieroshops Clutch||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||04-23-2000||10:17 PM||||Has anyone here tried Fieroshops Kevlar clutch, If so how is it? Is the pedal pressure harder than the stock pressure? Does it chatter at all upon engagement? What do you think of it? Anyone's commentary would be appreciated.<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||04-24-2000||02:10 AM||||88Formula, I have installed many clutches and finally replaced mine. I will say this, all thew clutches including the one I installed in my 88 GT have a light petal even though the clamp load is increased. Also this clutch does not slip. It is precise. If you want call me or e-mail me and I will provide you with several e-mail addresses so you can find out from them directly. These are people that have one of my clutches in their Fieros. I ahve not talked to these people and I will not ask them to give me a good recommendation unless they absolutly like thier clutch.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex4mula||04-24-2000||09:15 AM||||I just received my Kevlar clutch last thursday. Will be installing it sometime during May when I do my 3.4 conversion. Will update then. By now just can say that George (Fieroshop) is a very nice guy to deal with.||||reg||14
Z||000003||JohnnyB3||04-24-2000||01:33 PM||||Jusy blew my clutch in an 86 SE V6.<BR>Got quotes as high as $1,000.  Someone mentioned a PEP Boys $400 special so I called them.  $340.00 total price... Lifetime warranty for the disc, plate, fork, bearing, seal installed. ||||reg||14
Z||000004||JohnnyB3||04-24-2000||01:33 PM||||Jusy blew my clutch in an 86 SE V6.<BR>Got quotes as high as $1,000.  Someone mentioned a PEP Boys $400 special so I called them.  $340.00 total price... Lifetime warranty for the disc, plate, fork, bearing, seal installed. ||||reg||14
Z||000005||lennyb4||04-24-2000||02:23 PM||||Hey Johnny..If i was you i would call them back. I saw your post and called (i need a new set-up to). The $400.00 special is for labor anly they wanted another $200.00 for the clutch kit..Just thought id let you know before you get locked into something.||||reg||11
Z||000006||fieroshop||04-24-2000||11:54 PM||||Hey JohnnyB3, be careful and check out exactly what they are going to give you for that money, also all of the Pep Boys send me their customers who own Fieros. The reason they do that is that they are not allowed to work on Fieros. Also read the fine line and you will see that they state starting at||||reg||1
Z||000007||LarryB||04-25-2000||12:30 AM||||I went through this a few months ago when the clutch on my 2M4 went.<P>The $399 special is for "most" cars and includes labor and a kit with throwout bearing and reman clutch/pressure plate.  They have the same setup for "most" 4WD vehicles for $499.<P>The Fiero isn't on this "most" list and they quoted me a total of $641.45 to do the work, including nearly 8 hours labor.  It would be about another $20 to use a kit with new parts (which I'd recommend in any case).  I spoke to one of the mechanics there for about 10 minutes who had a clue about Fieros (that was a surprise!), he warned me that replacing the clutch on an L4 was a *****  compared to the V6. I can't speak to that but it is a *****   compared to doing the front-engine RWD cars I'd previously done.<P>It would have been worth it for me this time to have paid the ~$450 in labor for them to do it. YMMV.<P><BR>||||reg||1
